ାପଡ଼େ। The crow eats while the daughter-in-law receives the scolding. We can see the injustice before anyone explains it. The saying turns attention from the easiest person to blame towards what actually happened. Imagined occasion: A shared document goes missing, and the newest volunteer is blamed before anyone checks the folder history. 20. One hand cannot clap ଏକା ହାତରେ ତାଳି ବାଜେ ନାହିଁ A clap cannot sound with one hand alone. ଅର୍ଥ: କିଛି କାମ ପାଇଁ ଉଭୟ ପକ୍ଷର ସହଯୋଗ ଦରକାର; ଗୋଟିଏ ପକ୍ଷର ଚେଷ୍ଟାରେ ସବୁବେଳେ କାମ ହୁଏ ନାହିଁ। ତେବେ କ୍ଷତି ହେଲେ ଉଭୟ ପକ୍ଷ ସମାନ ଦୋଷୀ ବୋଲି ଧରିନେବା ଠିକ୍ ନୁହେଁ। Two palms make the sound together. It is a useful picture of cooperation when a task needs a response from someone else. It is not a rule that both people are equally responsible for harm, especially where one faces coercion or abuse. Imagined occasion: One person keeps proposing dates for a shared project; the other finally helps settle a workable plan."
