        "heading": "A regional name and its work",
        "text": "The Bhadrak District Gazetteer uses the name Sunari Bania for makers of gold and silver ornaments, including human and animal figurines. It also describes goldsmiths moving into agriculture. The passage gives no count or precise date for that change, but it preserves an important distinction: an inherited community identity can outlast a particular livelihood. The account belongs to Bhadrak. Its terminology cannot make every use of Bania across India equivalent, or identify the community of someone simply because they make jewellery. Names need their local histories as much as objects do.",
