        "heading": "Leave room for worship and looking",
        "text": "Ask about entry, footwear and photography when you arrive, and ask before photographing people. Keep doorways clear while you study a detail. If steps or uneven ground are a concern, describe your needs before making a special trip; the photographs here cannot confirm today’s accessible route. Allow a temple visit and a performance evening their own time. For the daytime visit, one arch, one roof comparison and one carving are enough to give you questions to carry into the next temple. You can then decide whether to continue through Bhubaneswar, pause for a meal or give Dhauli a separate visit."
