        "text": "In its 2019 catalogue, the museum includes mathematical equations woven using single ikat. It also discusses yarn preparation and cloth carrying verses from the Gita Govinda. Pattern begins before the finished cloth. What must a weaver plan while looking at yarn rather than a completed image? Carry that question into a textile gallery, and read the labels before linking any particular piece to the catalogue examples."
