    "practical": [
      {
        "heading": "Make time for the wetland",
        "text": "Mangalajodi rewards a visit built around watching birds. Its reed beds and shallow water provide habitat for resident and migratory species; Incredible India identifies November to February as the winter birdwatching season. That seasonal guide cannot predict what you will see on a particular day. Consider staying nearby if you want time to return to your notes between outings, or would rather avoid a long journey immediately before or after watching. If you only want one outing, compare an overnight stay with a day visit from your existing base. The useful question is how much unhurried time each arrangement leaves you."
      },
      {
        "heading": "A camp name is a starting point",
        "text": "Incredible India names Mangalajodi Nature Camp as an accommodation option. Treat that as a lead to investigate: this guide has not inspected its rooms or confirmed current operation, facilities or availability. Ask for the exact property name, map location and current photographs of the room and bathroom you would book. A photograph of birds tells you why someone might visit Mangalajodi; it tells you nothing about the bed, steps to a room or bathroom arrangements. Describe what your group needs in ordinary terms: whether someone finds steps difficult, needs a particular meal, or cannot sit comfortably in a boat for long. Ask for specific answers rather than relying on words such as “comfortable” or “accessible”."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Work out the room-to-water journey",
        "text": "Before paying, put the property location and the outing’s meeting point side by side. Ask who takes you between them, how you return and whether that journey is included in the quoted price. A room booking and a birdwatching booking may need separate arrangements. If you agree on an early start, ask how breakfast and checkout fit around it. For a late arrival, confirm whom to contact and how to find the entrance. Keep the accommodation contact and the guide’s contact separately, even if one person helps arrange both. Ask for a written breakdown of the room, meals, guide, boat and transfers, showing which are included and which cost extra. Check what happens to each part if weather changes the outing or you need to cancel."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Leave room for a quieter day",
        "text": "Do not make the value of the stay depend on a long list of sightings. Leave time to compare a few observations, look up a bird you could not identify, or discuss what you noticed with your guide. Those pauses can be part of the reason to stay. If part of your group will skip the boat trip, ask what they can comfortably do at the property while the others are away. Confirm somewhere suitable to rest and how meals will work. Choose the stay only when it works for the people travelling with you as well as the outing you have in mind."
      }
    ],
