        "text": "Satapada sits on the southeastern side of Chilika. The lagoon’s connection with the Bay of Bengal is part of the attraction here, alongside the possibility of seeing Irrawaddy dolphins. A boat outing can be a way to understand that meeting of waters, rather than a race between stops. Before choosing a boat, ask the operator to describe the route: where you will leave from, which places you will pass, where you can go ashore and how long the return will take. A trip described simply as “Chilika” leaves too much unanswered."
