        "heading": "A glimpse can be enough",
        "text": "The Chilika Development Authority cautions that visitors rarely see an entire Irrawaddy dolphin. A head or part of the tail may be all that appears above the water. That modest expectation is useful: a brief view is still an encounter with a wild animal, and an outing may bring no sighting at all. Ask your guide what to watch for before the search begins. If you see something, describe its shape and direction instead of pressing for a closer approach. Leave time to watch the water after the first glimpse. You do not need a photograph to have noticed something."
